                    <div class="tab-panel active" id="capybaras-tab-overview">
                        <h2 class="section-h2">Overview</h2>
                        <p>Capybaras brings the world's chillest animal to Minecraft. They can be found in swamp and mangrove biomes, and with a few sugar cane you can make one your own. Once tamed, you can equip them with cosmetics like a top hat, or protect them with iron, gold, or diamond armor.</p>
                        <p>With over 10 different capybara variants to find, each one feels a little different. When slain they drop capybara fur blocks that can be crafted into carpets, you can also shear the capybara to get the fur block.</p>
                        <p>Cosmetics and capybara armor can be found inside chests scattered around the world, so make sure to explore.</p>
                        <h2 class="section-h2" style="margin-top:2rem;">Highlights</h2>
                        <div class="feat-grid">
                            <div class="feat-card"><h4>Tame with Sugar Cane</h4><p>Find capybaras in swamp and mangrove biomes and tame them with sugar cane.</p></div>
                            <div class="feat-card"><h4>Cosmetics</h4><p>Dress up your tamed capybara with cosmetics like a top hat, found in chests around the world.</p></div>
                            <div class="feat-card"><h4>Capybara Armor</h4><p>Equip your capybara with iron, gold, or diamond armor to protect them from mobs.</p></div>
                            <div class="feat-card"><h4>10+ Variants</h4><p>Over 10 unique capybara variants to discover, each with their own look.</p></div>
                        </div>
                        <h2 class="section-h2" style="margin-top:2.5rem;">Contents</h2>
                        <div class="cat-list">
                            <div class="cat-list-title">Wiki Categories</div>
                            <ul>
                                <li><strong>Taming</strong> How to find and tame a capybara.</li>
                                <li><strong>Cosmetics</strong> All cosmetics and how to equip them.</li>
                                <li><strong>Armor</strong> The three armor tiers available for capybaras.</li>
                                <li><strong>Variants</strong> All known capybara variants.</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="tab-panel" id="capybaras-tab-taming">
                        <h2 class="section-h2">Taming</h2>
                        <p>Capybaras are passive mobs that roam swamp and mangrove biomes. They will never attack you.</p>
                        <div class="steps">
                            <div class="step-item"><div class="step-num">01</div><div><h4>Find a Capybara</h4><p>Head to a Swamp or Mangrove biome. Capybaras can usually be found hanging in or around water.</p></div></div>
                            <div class="step-item"><div class="step-num">02</div><div><h4>Bring Sugar Cane</h4><p>Sugar cane is the only thing a capybara can be tamed with. Grow or find some before you go looking for one.</p></div></div>
                            <div class="step-item"><div class="step-num">03</div><div><h4>Right Click to Feed</h4><p>Hold sugar cane and right click the capybara to feed it. You may need to do this multiple times before it becomes tamed.</p></div></div>
                            <div class="step-item"><div class="step-num">04</div><div><h4>Tamed</h4><p>Once tamed, the capybara will follow you. You can now equip it with cosmetics and armor or make it sit.</p></div></div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="tab-panel" id="capybaras-tab-cosmetics">
                        <h2 class="section-h2">Cosmetics</h2>
                        <p>Once your capybara is tamed, you can equip it with cosmetics. These are purely decorative and found inside chests scattered around the world.</p>
                        <div class="block-list">
                            <div class="block-entry"><img src="/img/capybaras/cosmetics/top_hat.png" alt="Top Hat" /><div class="block-entry-body"><h4>Top Hat</h4><p>A fancy top hat for your capybara. Found in chests around the world.</p></div></div>
                        </div>
                        <p style="margin-top:1.5rem;">More cosmetics can be found by exploring and looting chests. Keep an eye out while adventuring.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="tab-panel" id="capybaras-tab-armor">
                        <h2 class="section-h2">Armor</h2>
                        <p>Protect your tamed capybara with armor. There are three tiers available, each offering different levels of protection. Capybara armor is found in chests around the world, just like cosmetics.</p>
                        <table class="armor-table">
                            <thead><tr><th>Tier</th><th>Material</th><th>Where to Find</th></tr></thead>
                            <tbody>
                            <tr><td><span class="tier-badge tier-iron">Iron</span></td><td>Iron Capybara Armor</td><td>Chests around the world</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><span class="tier-badge tier-gold">Gold</span></td><td>Golden Capybara Armor</td><td>Chests around the world</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><span class="tier-badge tier-diamond">Diamond</span></td><td>Diamond Capybara Armor</td><td>Chests around the world</td></tr>
                            </tbody>
                        </table>
                    </div>
                    <div class="tab-panel" id="capybaras-tab-variants">
                        <h2 class="section-h2">Variants</h2>
                        <p>There are over 10 capybara variants to discover in the world. Each one has a unique appearance. Some may be rarer than others, so keep exploring.</p>
                        <div class="variants-grid">
                            <div class="variant-card"><img src="/img/capybaras/variants/capybara_brown.png" alt="Brown" /><div class="vname">Brown</div></div>
                            <div class="variant-card"><img src="/img/capybaras/variants/capybara_white.png" alt="White" /><div class="vname">White</div></div>
